# Responsive UI / UX

Every UI change and feature must work well on phone (~375px) and desktop. Prefer useful clarity over decorative chrome.

## Shell (ops app)

- **`md+`:** collapsible sidebar (`AppNav`)
- **`< md`:** bottom tabs (primary destinations) + **More** sheet — do not invent per-page nav
- Keep gym-floor actions (check-in, members, classes) in primary tabs when the role allows
- Respect bottom-bar clearance via `--ops-bottom-clearance` and `safe-area` tokens on fixed chrome

## Layout

```svelte
<!-- ❌ BAD — desktop-only density -->
<div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-6 p-8">

<!-- ✅ GOOD — stack first, expand later; prefer page spacing tokens; desktop uses ~5% side gutters -->
<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 p-[var(--spacing-page)] sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 lg:gap-6 lg:px-[var(--spacing-page-x-lg)] lg:py-[var(--spacing-page-lg)]">
```

- Touch targets ≥ `--touch-target` (44px); app shells use `.amrap-app-shell` (`dvh`)
- Desktop content uses full available width with `--spacing-page-x-lg` (~5% each side); avoid hard `max-w-6xl` page shells
- Avoid `min-w-[36rem]` tables without a mobile alternative (cards / stack / intentional scroll)
- One job per section; no competing chrome

## Design system

- Reuse `--color-*`, layout tokens in `layout.css`, shared `Input` / `Button` / `FormField` under `src/lib/components/ui/`
- No one-off visual forks or hardcoded product copy — `es` + `en` dictionaries
- Icon-only controls need `aria-label`; nav links use `aria-current` when active

